{"type":"tool_result","run_id":"run_ef50a0423a13","seq":19,"ts":"2026-10-30T11:33:40.543973Z","data":{"call_id":"chatcmpl-tool-619d0c10a37943b98d0aaad1a3a44b31","name":"describe_phenotype","ok":true,"error":null,"evidence_id":"e5","kind":"phenotype","summary":"Microscopist on 4 field(s): density lower vs DMSO; 7 observations; candidates: Microtubule stabilizers","image_ids":["f_e39ab479a5ab.composite","f_6c2d8d9f2508.composite","f_7f390bd32674.composite","f_5b254049b0b8.composite","f_b936a0c0d2e0.composite"],"data":{"field_ids":["f_e39ab479a5ab","f_6c2d8d9f2508","f_7f390bd32674","f_5b254049b0b8"],"dmso_field_ids":["f_b936a0c0d2e0"],"model":"meta-models/muse-spark-open-1026","images":"composites only","report":{"cell_density":"lower","observations":[{"channel":"composite","finding":"DMSO control f_b936a0c0d2e0 is heavily blurred/out-of-focus with dense monolayer, precluding detailed comparison, but even its in-focus regions show dim diffuse green/red/blue. All 4 treated fields are in focus, sparse, and show identical contrast settings with markedly brighter signal than control.","agrees_with_measurements":false},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"Beta-tubulin (green) in all treated fields f_e39ab479a5ab, f_6c2d8d9f2508 (0.03 uM) and f_7f390bd32674, f_5b254049b0b8 (0.3 uM) is very bright, forming thick perinuclear rings, cages and bundled cables/asters around nuclei. Not diffuse fine network as expected for DMSO. Effect stronger at 0.3 uM.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"tubulin","finding":"Tubulin texture is highly heterogeneous/high-contrast: bundled cables with very bright foci adjacent to dark background, vs diffuse control. Corresponds to increased variation and sharp bright structures.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"DNA (blue) nuclei are irregular, lobed, elongated and invaginated, with loss of round smooth border. Many cells show multilobed, fragmented or multinucleated/micronuclei appearance and paler blue staining over enlarged area.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"dna","finding":"Increased frequency of very large nuclei / polyploid cells with 2-3x normal nuclear area, often with multiple nuclear lobes caged by tubulin bundles. More frequent/prominent in 0.3 uM fields f_7f390bd32674/f_5b254049b0b8.","agrees_with_measurements":true},{"channel":"actin","finding":"F-actin (red) remains present as cortical rim and broad lamellipodial ruffles/spikes at cell periphery in all treated fields. No loss/fragmentation of actin; cells appear well-spread. No discrete actin puncta.","agrees_with_measurements":false},{"channel":"composite","finding":"Cell number per field reduced vs dense control; remaining cells are large, well-spread with low nuclear-to-cytoplasm ratio in composite (large red/green cytoplasm around enlarged blue nuclei). Dose-dependent increase in severity 0.03 to 0.3 uM.","agrees_with_measurements":true}],"notable_cells":[{"field_id":"f_e39ab479a5ab","x":450,"y":550,"why":"Example of enlarged irregular nucleus caged by bright green tubulin bundle ring with red cortical actin"},{"field_id":"f_5b254049b0b8","x":950,"y":250,"why":"Large cell with dense peripheral red actin fringe and intense green perinuclear tubulin aster"}],"candidate_mechanisms":[{"moa":"Microtubule stabilizers","why":"Strong dose-dependent increase in tubulin mean/std/GLCM-contrast (z=22-27, 22-38, 62-103) visible as bright bundled perinuclear tubulin cages with irregular enlarged/multilobed nuclei (form_factor z=-26/-27, solidity z=-19, eccentricity z=11-16, frac_large_nucleus z=6-7) classically seen with taxane-like stabilizers, not destabilizers which reduce tubulin signal"}],"uncertainty":"DMSO control is out-of-focus limiting actin morphometry comparison; no actin features provided to confirm actin is preserved"}},"cost_usd":0.02048}}
